\label{def:function variation}
Let $\mathcal{J}$ be the set of cost functions $J_t$, for $t=1,\dots,T$. 
The function variation $V_f$ is defined as drifts of the function sequences $\{J_t\}_{t=1}^T \in \mathcal{J}$  over the  horizon $T$, i.e.,  $  V_f= \sum_{t=2}^T \sup_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\mathbb{E}_\xi\big[|J_t(x,\xi) - J_{t-1}(x,\xi)| \big] $.

